  "question": {
    "text": "In a circuit, a metal filament lamp is connected in series with a capacitor of capacitance $\\mathrm{C} \\mu F$ across a $200 \\mathrm{~V}, 50 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ supply. The power consumed by the lamp is $500 \\mathrm{~W}$ while the voltage drop across it is $100 \\mathrm{~V}$. Assume that there is no inductive load in the circuit. Take $r m s$ values of the voltages. The magnitude of the phaseangle (in degrees) between the current and the supply voltage is $\\varphi$. Assume, $\\pi \\sqrt{3} \\approx 5$.<br>The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_c4e4f7157125.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 172px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>500</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Now current in the circuit,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>voltage</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>across</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>resistor</mi></mrow><mi>resistance</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Phasor diagram of the given circuit for voltage,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_9889948106dc.png\" style=\"width: 274px; height: 174px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>Now,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>200</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>and&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p>From the phasor diagram,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mi>&#981;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"
  }
